          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $M>0$ and let $\\mathcal H=\\Lambda^*\\mathbb C^2$ have orthonormal occupation basis $|n_1,n_2\\rangle$ for $n_1,n_2\\in\\{0,1\\}$. Define fermionic annihilation operators by $a_1|n_1,n_2\\rangle=n_1|0,n_2\\rangle$ and $a_2|n_1,n_2\\rangle=(-1)^{n_1}n_2|n_1,0\\rangle$, and let $a_\\alpha^*$ be their Hilbert adjoints. Set $P^0=MI$, $P^j=0$, all central charges to zero, and $Q_\\alpha=\\sqrt{2M}a_\\alpha$, $\\bar Q_{\\dot\\alpha}=Q_\\alpha^*$ with dotted index corresponding to the same $\\alpha$. Give $\\mathcal H$ the parity $(-1)^{n_1+n_2}$. This finite-dimensional rest fiber is a positive representation of the N=1 supercharge anticommutators in the stated mostly-plus convention; it has two even and two odd states. Use natural units $\\hbar=c=1$, so $M$ has mass dimension one and each displayed supercharge has mass dimension one-half. It is only a rest-algebra fiber and asserts no full spacetime representation.",
