            "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-trace-class-operator": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $\\omega>0$. Let the zero-energy subspace have dimensions $m_0^+=2$ and $m_0^-=1$, and let there be one positive-energy pair $\\mathcal H_\\omega^+=\\mathbb C|b\\rangle$ and $\\mathcal H_\\omega^-=\\mathbb C|f\\rangle$. Give the five-dimensional Hilbert space the orthonormal basis $|0_1\\rangle,|0_2\\rangle,|0_-\\rangle,|b\\rangle,|f\\rangle$ and parity $+1$ on $|0_1\\rangle,|0_2\\rangle,|b\\rangle$ and $-1$ on $|0_-\\rangle,|f\\rangle$. Define $Q=0$ on the three zero-energy states and $Q|b\\rangle=\\sqrt\\omega|f\\rangle$, $Q|f\\rangle=\\sqrt\\omega|b\\rangle$; set $H=Q^2$. For each $\\beta>0$, supply the diagonal operator $T_\\beta$ on the displayed basis by $T_\\beta|0_1\\rangle=|0_1\\rangle$, $T_\\beta|0_2\\rangle=|0_2\\rangle$, $T_\\beta|0_-\\rangle=|0_-\\rangle$, $T_\\beta|b\\rangle=e^{-\\beta\\omega}|b\\rangle$, and $T_\\beta|f\\rangle=e^{-\\beta\\omega}|f\\rangle$. The heat supertrace is $W(\\beta)=1$ for all $\\beta>0$.",
