          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Moore and Saxena, TASI Lectures on Topological Field Theories and Differential Cohomology",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.07408",
                "locator": "§23.3 PDF97–100 / printed96–99, especially (23.34)–(23.38); alternating homotopy-group measure, not an explicit proof of the local cochain gluing formula."
              },
              {
                "title": "Baez and Lauda, Higher-Dimensional Algebra V: 2-Groups",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0307200",
                "locator": "§8.3 pp.55–63; associator cocycle p.59 and monoidal coherence pp.60–61; explicit finite cochain 2-groupoid constructed locally."
              },
              {
                "title": "Benini, Cordova and Hsin, On 2-Group Global Symmetries and Their Anomalies",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1803.09336",
                "locator": "§2.3, printed pp.18–20 / PDF19–21; background and gauge equations only, explicit coherence reconstructed locally."
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "reference": "items/thm-aqft-finite-two-group-gauging-gluing.md",
          "statement": "Fix a finite group $G$, finite abelian group $A$, action $\\rho$, normalized $3$-cocycle $\\beta$, and a finite ordered simplicial complex $K$. Let $\\mathcal B(K)$ be the full background gauge $2$-groupoid, retaining its vertex $2$-gauge transformations, and let $W_K:\\operatorname{Ob}\\mathcal B(K)\\to U(1)$ be constant on $1$-arrows. Let $V_K,E_K$ be the numbers of vertices and edges and define\n\n$$\nc(K)=\\frac{|A|^{V_K-E_K}}{|G|^{V_K}}.\n$$\n\nThen its higher gauging sum satisfies\n\n$$\nZ_K^{(2)}(W_K)=\\sum_{[x]}W_K(x)\\frac{|\\pi_2(\\mathcal B(K),x)|}{|\\pi_1(\\mathcal B(K),x)|}=c(K)\\sum_{x\\in\\operatorname{Ob}\\mathcal B(K)}W_K(x).\n$$\n\nFor any subcomplex $L$ and fixed field $s$ on $L$, the higher sum over the relative $2$-groupoid is\n\n$$\nZ_{K,L}^{(2)}(s)=\\frac{c(K)}{c(L)}\\sum_{x|_L=s}W_K(x).\n$$\n\nIn particular let $K=K_1\\cup_\\Sigma K_2$, where the intersection is the subcomplex $\\Sigma$ and all orders are induced. Assume invariant weights $W_i$ and $W_K$ obey $W_K(x)=W_2(x|_{K_2})W_1(x|_{K_1})$. Put $Z_i(s)=Z_{K_i,\\Sigma}^{(2)}(s)$. These boundary functions are invariant on $1$-arrows of $\\mathcal B(\\Sigma)$ and obey the actual finite $2$-group gluing law\n\n$$\nZ_K^{(2)}(W_K)=\\sum_{[s]\\in\\pi_0\\mathcal B(\\Sigma)}Z_2(s)Z_1(s)\\frac{|\\pi_2(\\mathcal B(\\Sigma),s)|}{|\\pi_1(\\mathcal B(\\Sigma),s)|}.\n$$\n\nThe empty complex has $c=1$ and one empty field. For a point and unit weight the sum is $|A|/|G|$. When $A$ is trivial these formulas reduce to ordinary finite flat $G$-connection normalization. The theorem assumes scalar invariant weights and their stated factorization; it does not assert that an arbitrary higher cocycle defines such boundary scalar data.",
