          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $G$ be a complex reductive affine algebraic group, let $V$ be a finite-dimensional complex vector space with an algebraic representation $\\rho:G\\to\\operatorname{GL}(V)$, and let $N\\leq V$ be a linear subspace satisfying $\\rho(g)N=N$ for every $g\\in G$. Define $V^G=\\{v\\in V:\\rho(g)v=v\\text{ for all }g\\in G\\}$, give $V/N$ the induced representation, and let $\\pi:V\\to V/N$ be the quotient map. Then the restriction $\\pi^G:V^G\\to(V/N)^G$ is surjective and has kernel $V^G\\cap N$. Consequently the map\n\n$$\nV^G/(V^G\\cap N)\\longrightarrow(V/N)^G,\\qquad v+(V^G\\cap N)\\longmapsto v+N\n$$\n\nis a canonical complex-linear isomorphism.",
