          "statement": "Let $J=J_{\\bar 0}\\oplus J_{\\bar 1}$ be a finite-dimensional $\\mathbb Z/2$-graded complex vector space with a finite homogeneous basis $z_1,\\ldots,z_n$, each generator assigned a rational engineering weight. Form $P=\\operatorname{Sym}(J_{\\bar 0}^{*})\\otimes\\Lambda(J_{\\bar 1}^{*})$. For finite $q\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\geq0}$ and any $D\\in\\mathbb Q$, let $P_{q,D}$ be the span of supercommutative monomials of total generator degree at most $q$ and total engineering weight $D$. Then $P_{q,D}$ is finite-dimensional. If a group acts linearly on $J$ preserving parity and the weight grading, its invariant subspace $P_{q,D}^{G}$ is also finite-dimensional.",
