          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal A_U^{g,p}$ be the finite-jet horizontal-form spaces on a smooth open set $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$, with nilpotent BRST differential $s$, horizontal differential $d_H$, and $sd_H+d_Hs=0$. In bidegree $(1,4)$, define $H^{1,4}(s\\mid d_H)$ as the ghost-number-one four-forms $a_4$ satisfying $sa_4+d_Hb_3=0$ for some $b_3$, modulo the subspace $\\{sC_4+d_Hr_3:C_4\\in\\mathcal A_U^{0,4},\\ r_3\\in\\mathcal A_U^{1,3}\\}$. If a local counterterm changes an anomaly representative from $a_4$ to $a'_4=a_4+sC_4+d_Hr_3$, then $[a'_4]=[a_4]$ in $H^{1,4}(s\\mid d_H)$.",
