          "statement": "Let $n\\geq 1$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be nonempty and open, let $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional real Lie algebra, and let $V=V_{\\bar 0}\\oplus V_{\\bar 1}$ be a finite-dimensional graded complex vector space with an even Lie-algebra representation $\\rho:\\mathfrak g\\to\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$. Form the graded-commutative finite-jet algebra over $C^\\infty(U)$ from an even $\\mathfrak g$-valued local one-form $A=A_\\mu^aT_a\\,dx^\\mu$, a ghost $c=c^aT_a$ with odd components of ghost number one, and matter fields $\\psi^\\alpha$ of fixed component parity and ghost number zero. Let $D_\\mu$ be the total derivatives on coefficient functions and formal field jets, and let $s$ be the left odd derivation of ghost number one specified by $sA_\\mu=\\partial_\\mu c+[A_\\mu,c]$, $sc=-\\tfrac12[c,c]$, $s\\psi=-\\rho(c)\\psi$, and $s(D_I\\Phi)=D_I(s\\Phi)$ on every multi-index jet. Then $s^2=0$ on the entire finite-jet algebra and $sD_\\mu=D_\\mu s$ for each $\\mu$.",
