        {
          "id": "def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "mathematics",
          "title": "Local BRST Cohomology Modulo Total Derivatives",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex",
            "lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "Let $n\\geq1$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be nonempty and open, let $\\mathcal F_U$ be the finite-jet local algebra with nilpotent BRST derivation $s$ and commuting total derivatives $D_\\mu$, and let $dx^1,\\ldots,dx^n$ be anticommuting coordinate one-forms. For $g\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $0\\leq p\\leq n$, let $\\mathcal A_U^{g,p}$ be the space of local horizontal $p$-forms of ghost number $g$, namely finite sums of $dx^{\\mu_1}\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge dx^{\\mu_p}$ with coefficients in the ghost-number-$g$ part of $\\mathcal F_U$. Define the horizontal differential $d_H:=dx^\\mu D_\\mu$; its square is $d_H^2a=dx^\\mu\\wedge dx^\\nu D_\\mu D_\\nu a=\\tfrac12dx^\\mu\\wedge dx^\\nu[D_\\mu,D_\\nu]a=0$. Extend $s$ to horizontal forms by $s(dx^\\mu\\wedge a)=-dx^\\mu\\wedge sa$. Since $sD_\\mu=D_\\mu s$, one has $s(d_Ha)=-dx^\\mu\\wedge D_\\mu(sa)=-d_H(sa)$, hence $sd_H+d_Hs=0$.\n\nFor $p=0$, set $\\mathcal A_U^{g,-1}=\\{0\\}$. The local BRST cohomology modulo total derivatives in bidegree $(g,p)$ is\n\n$$H^{g,p}(s\\mid d_H):=\\frac{\\{a\\in\\mathcal A_U^{g,p}:\\text{there is }b\\in\\mathcal A_U^{g+1,p-1}\\text{ with }sa+d_Hb=0\\}}{\\{sm+d_Hn:m\\in\\mathcal A_U^{g-1,p},\\ n\\in\\mathcal A_U^{g,p-1}\\}}.$$\n\nThe denominator is a subspace of the numerator: for $a=sm+d_Hn$, choose $b=sn$ and compute $sa+d_Hb=s^2m+sd_Hn+d_Hsn=0$. For $p=0$, $n=b=0$ and the same verification reduces to $s^2m=0$. This is cohomology of the specified local jet algebra and horizontal differential; it is not cohomology of a physical state space or Hilbert space. Interpreting $d_H$-exact top forms as equal local functionals additionally assumes compact support or boundary conditions that make the corresponding surface term vanish.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
