          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "statement": "Assume countable choice. Let $M$ be a compact smooth Riemannian manifold without boundary, $n=\\dim M>0$, and $E$ a finite-rank Hermitian bundle. Let $P:C^\\infty(M,E)\\to C^\\infty(M,E)$ be a smooth second-order differential operator. In local coordinates and a bundle frame, write $P=\\sum_{|\\alpha|\\le2}a_\\alpha(x)\\partial_x^\\alpha$ and define its positive-frequency principal symbol by $p(x,\\xi)=\\sum_{|\\alpha|=2}a_\\alpha(x)(i\\xi)^\\alpha$ (equivalently, the coefficient of $\\lambda^2$ in $e^{-i\\lambda f}P(e^{i\\lambda f}v)$ at $df_x=\\xi$). Suppose $p(x,\\xi)$ is a Hermitian matrix satisfying $p(x,\\xi)\\ge c|\\xi|^2I$ for some $c>0$. Assume its nonnegative selfadjoint realization has a complete orthonormal basis of smooth eigensections and a smooth heat kernel $K_t(y,z):E_z\\to E_y$ relative to Riemannian volume. No scalar-principal-symbol hypothesis is imposed. In normal coordinates and smooth unitary frames based at $x$, set\n\n$$k_x(w)=(2\\pi)^{-n}\\int_{\\mathbb R^n}e^{iw\\cdot\\xi}e^{-p(x,\\xi)}\\,d\\xi.$$\n\nThen $k_x$ is Schwartz, meaning it is smooth and $p_{\\alpha,\\beta}(k_x)=\\sup_{w\\in\\mathbb R^n}\\|w^\\alpha\\partial_w^\\beta k_x(w)\\|<\\infty$ for every pair of multi-indices $\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb N_0^n$, $\\int k_x(w)\\,dw=I$, and, locally uniformly for bounded $a,b\\in T_xM$,\n\n$$t^{n/2}K_t(\\exp_x(\\sqrt t\\,a),\\exp_x(\\sqrt t\\,b))\\longrightarrow k_x(a-b).$$\n\nFor every integer $L>n$ there is $C_L$ such that\n\n$$\\|K_t(y,z)\\|\\le C_Lt^{-n/2}(1+d(y,z)/\\sqrt t)^{-L}\\qquad(0<t\\le1).$$\n\nIn dimension zero the corresponding assertion is the finite-dimensional limit $K_t(x,x)\\to I$ and zero kernel between distinct points.",
