            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "Assume countable choice. Let $T=(\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z)^r$, $r\\ge0$, be a compact torus acting smoothly by isometries on a compact Riemannian manifold $M$ without boundary. Let $E^0,\\ldots,E^N$ be finite-rank Hermitian bundles and, for $0\\le j<N$, let $d_j:C^\\infty(M,E^j)\\to C^\\infty(M,E^{j+1})$ be first-order differential maps with $d_{j+1}d_j=0$. Assume the principal-symbol sequence is exact for every nonzero real cotangent vector. Suppose a jointly smooth unitary bundle action has fiber maps $\\rho_t^j(x):E_x^j\\to E_{t\\cdot x}^j$ satisfy $\\rho_e^j(x)=I_{E_x^j}$ and $\\rho_{st}^j(x)=\\rho_s^j(t\\cdot x)\\circ\\rho_t^j(x)$; on sections set $(U_t^j s)(y)=\\rho_t^j(t^{-1}\\cdot y)(s(t^{-1}\\cdot y))$ and require $U_t^{j+1}d_j=d_jU_t^j$. Put $d_{-1}=d_N=0$, $E^{\\mathrm{ev}}=\\bigoplus_{j\\text{ even}}E^j$, $E^{\\mathrm{odd}}=\\bigoplus_{j\\text{ odd}}E^j$, $d=\\bigoplus_jd_j$, and $\\Delta=(d+d^*)^2$, where $d^*$ is the formal adjoint for the chosen metrics and Riemannian volume. For the nonnegative selfadjoint Hodge realization on $L^2$, assume that $\\Delta$ has discrete spectrum, smooth eigensections, a trace-class heat operator $e^{-t\\Delta}$ with smooth kernel for every $t>0$, finite-dimensional cohomology, and a harmonic representative for each cohomology class. For $g\\in T$, let $M^g=\\{x\\in M:g\\cdot x=x\\}$, and suppose each $x\\in M^g$ is simple, meaning $I-dg_x:T_xM\\to T_xM$ is invertible. Then\n\n$$\\lim_{t\\downarrow0}\\operatorname{Str}(U_g e^{-t\\Delta})=\\sum_{x\\in M^g}\\frac{\\sum_{j=0}^N(-1)^j\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho_g^j|_{E_x^j})}{|\\det_{\\mathbb R}(I-dg_x)|}.$$\n\nHere $\\operatorname{Str}$ is the trace on $E^{\\mathrm{ev}}$ minus the trace on $E^{\\mathrm{odd}}$. The simplicity condition makes $M^g$ a finite set; the determinant is the normal Jacobian at that isolated fixed point.",
