          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $N\\geq0$ and put $R_N=\\mathbb C[\\epsilon]/(\\epsilon^{N+1})$. For each regulator $\\rho$, let $X_\\rho=X_\\rho^{\\bar 0}\\oplus X_\\rho^{\\bar 1}$ be the finite-dimensional graded field-coordinate space in the regulated perturbative LSZ amplitude datum. Its even coordinates are commuting, its odd coordinates generate the specified exterior algebra, and its source $J$ has commuting even components and anticommuting odd components paired in the declared order. Let $\\mathcal I_\\rho$ be the specified integration functional, consisting of the even-coordinate functional and ordered coefficient extraction over the odd coordinates, and let $S_{\\rho,\\epsilon}$ be an even action in its domain. Define\n$$\nZ_{\\rho,\\epsilon}[J]=\\mathcal I_\\rho\\!\\left(\\exp\\!\\bigl(iS_{\\rho,\\epsilon}(\\varphi)+i\\langle J,\\varphi\\rangle\\bigr)\\right).\n$$\nLet $F_{\\rho,\\epsilon}$ be the actual parity-preserving local formal coordinate map used at regulator $\\rho$, with $F_{\\rho,0}=\\operatorname{id}$ and an inverse modulo $\\epsilon^{N+1}$. Use the full pullback $S_{\\rho,\\epsilon}\\circ F_{\\rho,\\epsilon}$, retaining every term through order $N$, and define\n$$\nZ'_{\\rho,\\epsilon}[J]=\\mathcal I_\\rho\\!\\left(\\exp\\!\\bigl(iS_{\\rho,\\epsilon}(F_{\\rho,\\epsilon}(\\psi))+i\\langle J,F_{\\rho,\\epsilon}(\\psi)\\rangle\\bigr)\\mathcal J_{F,\\rho}(\\psi)\\right),\n$$\nwhere the full graded Jacobian factor satisfies\n$$\n\\mathcal I_\\rho(h(\\varphi))=\\mathcal I_\\rho\\!\\left(h(F_{\\rho,\\epsilon}(\\psi))\\,\\mathcal J_{F,\\rho}(\\psi)\\right)\n$$\nfor every admissible integrand $h$. Assume $Z_{\\rho,\\epsilon}[0]$ is a unit for each $\\rho$, and that for the same ordered field components the connected Green functions defined by the graded source derivatives have a common regulator limit with stable external channels $a_j$, masses $m_{a_j}>0$, and nonzero simple-pole residues $Z_{a_j}$ at $s_j=m_{a_j}^2$, where $s_j=-\\eta^{\\mu\\nu}p_{j,\\