          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Use natural units $c=\\hbar=1$ on four-dimensional Minkowski space $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$. Let $\\phi\\in C^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$ be a real, Grassmann-even (commuting) scalar field of engineering dimension one, with a stable one-particle state of pole mass $m>0$; here stable means an isolated real mass pole with zero decay width. Stability and the existence of this state are physical input data; no construction of a state is asserted. An effective field theory (EFT) here is the selected local low-energy representative organized in powers of its cutoff; its exact amplitude is separate supplied model data. For the finite-jet local-operator convention, use the complexification for the finite-jet algebra and impose the usual reality condition on $\\phi$. Take one field species, maximum jet order $r=1$, polynomial degree at most $q=4$, weight $D=8$, and trivial internal group. Specify the spacetime-index action as follows. Let\n\n$$L_{\\mathbb R}=\\{\\Lambda\\in\\operatorname{GL}_4(\\mathbb R):\\Lambda^{T}\\eta\\Lambda=\\eta\\},\\qquad L_{\\mathbb C}=\\{\\Lambda\\in\\operatorname{GL}_4(\\mathbb C):\\Lambda^{T}\\eta\\Lambda=\\eta\\}.$$\n\nThe real Lorentz group $L_{\\mathbb R}$ acts on coordinates by $x'^{\\mu}=\\Lambda^{\\mu}{}_{\\nu}x^{\\nu}$ and on the scalar field by $(\\Lambda\\cdot\\phi)(x)=\\phi(\\Lambda^{-1}x)$, so its field-value representation is trivial. For $0\\le s\\le r$, its induced action on derivative components is\n\n$$\\partial_{\\mu_1}\\cdots\\partial_{\\mu_s}(\\Lambda\\cdot\\phi)(x)=(\\Lambda^{-1})^{\\nu_1}{}_{\\mu_1}\\cdots(\\Lambda^{-1})^{\\nu_s}{}_{\\mu_s}(\\partial_{\\nu_1}\\cdots\\partial_{\\nu_s}\\phi)(\\Lambda^{-1}x),$$\n\nwith the empty product for $s=0$ giving the scalar field itself. Use the complexification of these tensor representations, with $L_{\\mathbb C}$, on the finite-jet polynomial algebra in the supplier's invariant construction; this specifies its spacetime