          "statement": "On natural-unit Minkowski space $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and orientation $dx^0\\wedge dx^1\\wedge dx^2\\wedge dx^3$, take the trivial $H=SU(3)\\times U(1)_V$ bundle, zero $SU(3)$ background, and a smooth compactly supported real nondynamical $U(1)_V$ connection $B$ with $G=dB$. Let $\\alpha,\\theta\\in C_c^\\infty(M,\\mathbb R)$. Use the model's source-signed chirality convention $\\gamma_5=-i\\gamma^0\\gamma^1\\gamma^2\\gamma^3=i\\gamma_0\\gamma_1\\gamma_2\\gamma_3$, with positive chirality meaning eigenvalue $+1$. Use the model's Grassmann-odd coefficient algebra and conjugation for both Weyl fields: one smooth compactly supported positive-chirality Weyl field in $(\\mathbf1,+1)$, one smooth compactly supported neutral negative-chirality mass partner, and the charge-one scalar $\\Phi=v e^{i\\theta}$ in the Yukawa term $-y\\Phi\\bar\\psi_+\\psi_-+\\mathrm{h.c.}$, where $v>0$, $y\\ne0$, and $M_H=|y|v$. Fix the transformations $B\\mapsto B+d\\alpha$, $\\psi_+\\mapsto e^{-i\\alpha}\\psi_+$, $\\psi_-\\mapsto\\psi_-$, and $\\theta\\mapsto\\theta-\\alpha$, and use the consistent-anomaly representative with no non-invariant local counterterm. For any fixed integer $n\\geq1$, consider a specified $n$-point background-field vertex of $\\Gamma_H$ with insertions from components of $B$ and/or $\\theta$, and incoming real coordinate covectors $p_j=(p_{j0},p_{j1},p_{j2},p_{j3})\\in\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ satisfying $\\sum_{j=1}^n p_j=0$; set $E=\\max_{1\\leq j\\leq n,\\,0\\leq\\mu\\leq3}|p_{j\\mu}|$. No on-shell condition is imposed. Require $E/M_H\\ll1$ only for the low-energy effective-field-theory interpretation of that vertex. This condition applies to its finite set of external legs, not to the Fourier support of the compactly supported backgrounds, and gives no expansion-remainder bound; the exact local anomaly identity below is independent of it.\n\nAdopt the source-derived consistent-anomaly formula for a positiv