          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "physical_scope": "A conditional deduction for a fixed gauge-bundle sector of the source-qualified Euclidean N=4 SU(2) model on the round S4, only after a separately supplied finite-dimensional Q-preserving regulator satisfies the stated hypotheses. It proves neither that such a regulator exists for the source's formal S4 construction nor a continuum measure, t-to-infinity saddle limit, regulator-removal theorem, or empirical claim.",
          "statement": "Use natural units $c=\\hbar=1$ and fix one bundle sector of the adopted massless $\\mathcal N=4$ $SU(2)$ Yang–Mills model on the round Euclidean four-sphere $S^4_r$, with $r>0$ a length. The adopted background fixes the action, contour, field content, and total gauge-fixed odd transformation $Q=s+\\delta$; on its fields and ghosts the square is $Q^2=\\delta_{\\rm gauge}(a_0)+\\delta_{U(1)}(\\omega)$, where $a_0\\in\\mathfrak h_P=\\ker D_{A_*}$ is the declared parallel background zero mode and $\\delta_{U(1)}(\\omega)=-\\mathcal L_v^{\\mathrm{lift}}-\\delta_R$ is the combined lifted spacetime/R action, not a second copy of a gauge-covariant Lie derivative. The nongauge action on ghosts is $\\rho_{\\mathrm{gh}}(\\omega)=-\\mathcal L_v^{\\mathrm{lift}}$, and its auxiliary-index action is the one fixed by the source off-shell square. The source-ordered bilinear is $R^Q_{AB}=2\\epsilon\\widetilde\\Gamma_{AB}\\widetilde\\epsilon$ and the cohomological parameter is $\\phi=-(v^\\mu A_\\mu-\\beta_{v,P}+v^A\\Phi_A)$, where $\\beta_{v,P}$ is the fixed lift's vertical coefficient. The adopted affine ghost rule is $\\delta\\phi=-[c,\\phi]+\\rho_{\\mathrm{gh}}(\\omega)c$. Sectorwise gauge fixing is the $Q$-completed background-gauge insertion $Q\\Psi_{\\mathrm{gf}}$ with its specified ghost and zero-mode domains. This is a physical model assumption, not a deduction that the formal continuum functional integral exists.\n\nFor a fixed regulator label $\\rho$, assume that a finite-dimensional regulator of this model is supplied by an oriented smooth field-parameter manifold $\\mathfrak F_\\rho$ of finite dimension $n$, a smooth positive volume form $\\mu_\\rho$, and integration over the whole cycle $\\mathfrak F_\\rho$. Let $\\mathcal A_\\rho=\\Omega^\\bullet(\\mathfrak F_\\rho;\\mathbb C)$, let $I_\\rho(F)=\\int_{\\mathfrak F_\\rho}F_{[n]}$ be the integral of the degree-$n$ part, and let $Q_\\rho$ be the induced smooth odd derivation. The regulator must preserve the stated total $Q$ action and its square; no regulator existence or regulator-preservation claim is assumed. Let $J\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval of dimensionless deformation parameters. Let $S_\\rho,O_\\rho\\in\\mathcal A_\\rho$ be even, let $V_\\rho\\in\\mathcal A_\\rho$ be odd, and define $E_{\\rho,t}=e^{-S_\\rho-tQ_\\rho V_\\rho}$. In units with $\\hbar=1$, assume the regulated action $S_\\rho$ and deformation $tQ_\\rho V_\\rho$ are dimensionless. Assume $Q_\\rho S_\\rho=Q_\\rho O_\\rho=0$ and $(Q_\\rho^2V_\\rho)E_{\\rho,t}=0$ for every $t\\in J$. Assume the regulated measure and cycle are Q-invariant on the admissible integrands, in the exact sense that $I_\\rho(Q_\\rho(O_\\rho V_\\rho E_{\\rho,t}))=0$ for every $t\\in J$, with no anomaly or boundary contribution.\n\nWrite $(O_\\rho E_{\\rho,t})_{[n]}=f_{\\rho,t}\\mu_\\rho$ and assume $f_{\\rho,t}\\in L^1(\\mathfrak F_\\rho,\\mu_\\rho)$ for every $t\\in J$. Assume there is a measurable $\\mu_\\rho$-null set $N_\\rho\\subseteq\\mathfrak F_\\rho$ such that, for every $x\\in\\mathfrak F_\\rho\\setminus N_\\rho$, the map $t\\mapsto f_{\\rho,t}(x)$ is differentiable at every $t\\in J$. For $x\\notin N_\\rho$ define\n\n$$\\partial_t f_{\\rho,t}(x):=\\lim_{\\substack{h\\to0\\\\h\\in\\mathbb R,\\ h\\ne0,\\ t+h\\in J}}\\frac{f_{\\rho,t+h}(x)-f_{\\rho,t}(x)}{h}\\in\\mathbb C,$$\n\nand define $\\partial_t f_{\\rho,t}(x)=0$ for $x\\in N_\\rho$. Require $x\\mapsto\\partial_t f_{\\rho,t}(x)$ to be measurable for every $t\\in J$. For every compact $K\\subset J$, assume one nonnegative $g_K\\in L^1(\\mathfrak F_\\rho,\\mu_\\rho)$ and one $\\mu_\\rho$-null set $N_{\\rho,K}$ such that, for every $x\\notin N_{\\rho,K}$ and every $t\\in K$,\n\n$$|f_{\\rho,t}(x)|\\le g_K(x),\\qquad |\\partial_t f_{\\rho,t}(x)|\\le g_K(x).$$\n\nThen\n\n$$Z_\\rho(t):=I_\\rho(O_\\rho E_{\\rho,t})$$\n\nis constant on $J$, and for every $t\\in J$,\n\n$$Z_\\rho'(t)=-I_\\rho(O_\\rho(Q_\\rho V_\\rho)E_{\\rho,t})=-I_\\rho(Q_\\rho(O_\\rho V_\\rho E_{\\rho,t}))=0.$$\n\nThe conclusion applies only to this fixed finite-dimensional regulator and fixed bundle sector at finite $t$. The adopted S4 postulate does not construct the finite-dimensional data above, and this result supplies no infinite-dimensional continuum identity, $t\\to\\infty$ localization limit, or regulator-removal theorem.",
