          "statement": "Fix a finite jet order $r$, maximum polynomial field degree $q$, engineering weight $D$, finite field-species list, coefficient field $\\mathbb C$, and complex reductive affine algebraic group $G$ with the finite-dimensional rational action specified on the jet generators, including the declared spacetime-index symmetries. Let $W_D$ be the finite-dimensional space of all local polynomials of weight $D$ and degree at most $q$, before imposing $G$-invariance, and let $V_D=W_D^G$ be its invariant scalar subspace. An admitted raw relation space is a specified $G$-stable linear subspace $\\widetilde R_D\\leq W_D$, given by explicit linear identities among the chosen polynomials. Its invariant part is $R_D=\\widetilde R_D\\cap V_D$. Any action, boundary, or observable interpretation of the selected identities is extra mathematical data and must be stated with the result that verifies it.\n\nThe finite-order invariant operator-basis quotient is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal Q_D:=V_D/R_D.\n$$\n\nTwo invariant operators represent the same class exactly when their difference lies in $R_D$. An operator basis is any finite list of representatives in $V_D$ of a vector-space basis of $\\mathcal Q_D$. The quotient records precisely the declared relation space; it does not assert that every relation relevant to an arbitrary EFT, observable, or infinite operator tower has been included.",
