      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-aqft-topological-defect",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "physics",
          "library": "physics",
          "category": "advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry",
          "title": "Topological defect insertion in a specified model",
          "reference": "items/def-aqft-topological-defect.md",
          "design_state": "Assigned A-page definition authored from the exact future item contract.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "deps": [],
          "dependency_roles": {},
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix an integer $d\\ge1$ and a smooth $d$-manifold $M$, possibly with boundary. Fix the metric and signature, orientation and any time orientation, the geometric background bundles or lifts required by the model, and the boundary conditions. A **selected model** $\\mathcal T$ on $M$ consists of a specified configuration space $\\mathcal C_{\\mathcal T}(M)$ of fields, including each field bundle, regularity class, and admissible boundary behavior; a collection of local observables with their types and supports; a set $\\mathcal B_{\\mathcal T}$ of admissible combined background and boundary data; and a set $\\mathcal A_{\\mathcal T}$ of admissible complete insertion inputs. An element of $\\mathcal A_{\\mathcal T}$ records data $b\\in\\mathcal B_{\\mathcal T}$ and a finite ordered list whose entries are local observable insertions or other model-declared insertion data, together with the model's admissibility conditions on supports and labels. The model supplies a value space $\\mathcal V_{\\mathcal T}$ with a specified topology and a correlator functional $C_{\\mathcal T}:\\mathcal A_{\\mathcal T}\\to\\mathcal V_{\\mathcal T}$ with an explicit normalization convention, which may be normalized or unnormalized; the notation $C_{\\mathcal T}(b;D;X_1,\\ldots,X_n)$ denotes its value on the complete input with combined background and boundary data $b$, defect data $D$, and other insertion data $X_i$. The model also fixes its unit system, action and charge normalizations, and any regulator, measure, or renormalization prescription used to define $C_{\\mathcal T}$. These are model inputs: this definition does not construct them or assume a general interacting continuum theory exists.\n\nA **defect insertion** in $\\mathcal T$ is data $(j,\\lambda)$ where $j:\\Sigma\\hookrightarrow M^\\circ$ is a smooth embedding of a manifold $\\Sigma$ without boundary whose image is closed in the interior $M^\\circ=M\\setminus\\partial M$, and $\\lambda$ is the complete model-specified field, operator, or boundary-condition data supported on $j(\\Sigma)$, including any orientation, coorientation, framing, or label-transport rule the model requires. Its codimension is $d-\\dim\\Sigma$. It is an allowed entry of $\\mathcal A_{\\mathcal T}$ only when the model defines $C_{\\mathcal T}(b;D_{j,\\lambda};O_1,\\ldots,O_n)$ for each stated admissible combined background and boundary datum $b$ and list of other insertions.\n\nA **defect network** is data $D=(K,\\{S_s,j_s,\\lambda_s\\}_{s\\in S},\\{J_t\\}_{t\\in J})$ in which $K\\subset M^\\circ$ is closed, $S$ is finite, $K=\\bigsqcup_{s\\in S}S_s$ is a smooth stratification, and each $j_s:\\Sigma_s\\to S_s$ is a diffeomorphism from a smooth manifold without boundary onto its locally closed embedded stratum. The closure of each stratum is a union of strata, with the frontier condition that if $S_t$ meets the closure of $S_s$ and $S_t\\ne S_s$, then $S_t$ lies in that closure and has smaller dimension; the incidence relation records exactly these pairs. Each stratum carries its complete model-specified field, operator, boundary, orientation, coorientation, framing, and other label data $\\lambda_s$ as required; $J\\subseteq S$ is the set of junction strata, and each $S_t$ with $t\\in J$ carries a model-specified junction operator $J_t$ with an ordering of all incident labels. The model must declare which such networks and other insertions form admissible inputs of $\\mathcal A_{\\mathcal T}$ and define their correlators. A one-stratum network with no junction stratum is the preceding single defect, and a list of strata or a picture without its field and junction data is not a defect insertion.\n\nAn **isotopy** of a defect network is a smooth one-parameter family of its stratum embeddings $j_{s,t}:\\Sigma_s\\hookrightarrow M^\\circ$, $t\\in[0,1]$, compatible on stratum closures and incidence data, whose stratification and incidence relation are unchanged and which creates no additional intersections. The model-specified transport maps carry every stratum label $\\lambda_s$, framing or orientation, and junction operator along the family; the combined background and boundary data remain fixed, and the network stays disjoint from every other insertion throughout the deformation. A single-stratum defect is the one-element special case. The insertion is **topological in $\\mathcal T$** if, for every complete admissible input containing the selected network, every other insertion data $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ in that input (each of which may itself be an observable or another defect/network), and every such decorated isotopy from $D_0$ to $D_1$ disjoint from all the other insertion data, the model-defined correlators satisfy\n\n$$C_{\\mathcal T}(b;D_0;X_1,\\ldots,X_n)=C_{\\mathcal T}(b;D_1;X_1,\\ldots,X_n).$$\n\nThis is a property to verify for the specified model and insertion, not an automatic consequence of assigning a defect label or drawing a crossing. No physical quantity with units is introduced here; all dimensional quantities and normalizations remain those declared by $\\mathcal T$.",
          "physical_scope": "A definition for a named field-theory or quantum model whose admissible configurations and correlation functionals are specified; it asserts neither existence of a general continuum QFT nor realization of any proposed defect.",
