          "statement": "Use natural units $c=\\hbar=1$. Let $M$ be a compact oriented smooth four-manifold with a Riemannian metric and with the spin, gauge, matter, auxiliary, and R-symmetry bundles supplied as part of a rigid-background package. For each declared field species $a$, let $E_a\\to M$ be its specified vector bundle. Assign each species a parity $p(a)\\in\\{\\bar 0,\\bar 1\\}$, including a separate parity for every auxiliary and ghost species, and put $E^{\\bar j}=\\bigoplus_{p(a)=\\bar j}E_a$. Physical bosons are even and physical fermions are odd; ghosts may have either declared parity. The grading is parity modulo two. Write $\\Gamma^\\infty(M,E)$ for the space of smooth sections of a bundle $E\\to M$, with the topology of uniform convergence of every covariant derivative. A connection is an affine variable, represented by its difference from a fixed reference connection, an adjoint-valued one-form. Smooth sections are the common classical domain unless a different domain is stated.\n\nFor linearization, supply a local graded field chart at the chosen configuration $\\Phi_*$. Its even coordinates range over an open neighborhood of zero in a specified closed real linear subspace $V^{\\bar 0}$ of the even section space; its odd coordinates are formal anticommuting variables with values in a specified closed linear subspace $V^{\\bar 1}$ of the odd section space. Complex fields may be regarded as real pairs, with a declared complexification when required by $Q$. In this chart $\\Phi_*$ has coordinate zero and the tangent fluctuations are $V=V^{\\bar 0}\\oplus V^{\\bar 1}$. Require the chart, its inverse onto its image, and the coefficient maps of $Q$ to be smooth: all iterated directional derivatives in the even variables exist and are jointly continuous in the base point and directions; dependence on odd variables is specified by continuous alternating multilinear coefficient maps, smooth in the even variables. Taylor expansions below are formal jets 