          "physical_scope": "A conditional deduction for a fixed gauge-bundle sector of the source-qualified Euclidean N=4 SU(2) model on the round S4, only after a separately supplied finite-dimensional Q-preserving regulator satisfies the stated hypotheses. It proves neither that such a regulator exists for the source's formal S4 construction nor a continuum measure, t-to-infinity saddle limit, regulator-removal theorem, or empirical claim.",
          "statement": "Use natural units $c=\\hbar=1$ and fix one bundle sector of the adopted massless $\\mathcal N=4$ $SU(2)$ Yang–Mills model on the round Euclidean four-sphere $S^4_r$, with $r>0$ a length. The adopted background fixes the action, contour, field content, and total gauge-fixed odd transformation $Q=s+\\delta$; on its fields and ghosts the square is $Q^2=\\delta_{\\rm gauge}(a_0)+\\delta_{U(1)}(\\omega)$, where $a_0\\in\\mathfrak h_P=\\ker D_{A_*}$ is the declared parallel background zero mode and $\\delta_{U(1)}(\\omega)=-\\mathcal L_v^{\\mathrm{lift}}-\\delta_R$ is the combined lifted spacetime/R action, not a second copy of a gauge-covariant Lie derivative. The nongauge action on ghosts is $\\rho_{\\mathrm{gh}}(\\omega)=-\\mathcal L_v^{\\mathrm{lift}}$, and its auxiliary-index action is the one fixed by the source off-shell square. The source-ordered bilinear is $R^Q_{AB}=2\\epsilon\\widetilde\\Gamma_{AB}\\widetilde\\epsilon$ and the cohomological parameter is $\\phi=-(v^\\mu A_\\mu-\\beta_{v,P}+v^A\\Phi_A)$, where $\\beta_{v,P}$ is the fixed lift's vertical coefficient. The adopted affine ghost rule is $\\delta\\phi=-[c,\\phi]+\\rho_{\\mathrm{gh}}(\\omega)c$. Sectorwise gauge fixing is the $Q$-completed background-gauge insertion $Q\\Psi_{\\mathrm{gf}}$ with its specified ghost and zero-mode domains. This is a physical model assumption, not a deduction that the formal continuum functional integral exists.\n\nFor a fixed regulator label $\\rho$, assume that a finite-dimensional regulator of this model is supplied by an oriented smooth field-parameter manifold $\\mathfrak F_\\rho$ of finite dimension $n$, a smooth positive volume form $\\mu_\\rho$, and integration over the whole cycle $\\mathfrak F_\\rho$. Let $\\mathcal A_\\rho=\\Omega^\\bullet(\\mathfrak F_\\rho;\\mathbb C)$, let $I_\\rho(F)=\\int_{\\mathfrak F_\\rho}F_{[n]}$ be the integral of the degree-$n$ part, and let $Q_\\rho$ be a smooth odd derivation. Supply a smooth parity-preserving