          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume ZF together with the Axiom of Choice. Let $M=S^3$ or $S^4$, let $N\\ge2$, take the trivial principal right $SU(N)$-bundle $P=M\\times SU(N)$, and use its zero connection as affine origin. For any integer $j\\ge1$ and any continuous sphere family $f:S^j\\to\\mathcal A_\\infty^*$ of smooth connections on $P$, the cone formula $F([r,x])=r f(x)$ extends $f$ continuously over $D^{j+1}$ in the full affine connection space. The apex is the zero connection, whose holonomy group is the identity and which preserves every complex line, so this affine filling is reducible and does not lie entirely in $\\mathcal A_\\infty^*$. Relative avoidance changes the filling while fixing its boundary and produces a filling in $\\mathcal A_\\infty^*$; contraction of the disk to any chosen boundary point gives a based nullhomotopy. The weak-contractibility theorem ensures that such families exist for the trivial bundle and that their based homotopy classes vanish.",
